      en: "Trisul is a notable mountain in the Indian state of Uttarakhand. A group of three Himalayan mountain peaks in Uttarakhand, the highest of which reaches 7,120 metres. Regionally it captures the diversity and complexity of this part of India. Several characteristic features stand out: The name means 'trident', the weapon of Shiva. Was the first peak over 7,000m to be climbed (1907). In this sense, Trisul is one of the characteristic examples of Uttarakhand and of India as a whole. Geography K7 — Relief features and natural regions of India."
